#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:82
msgid "Deterministic helpers with explicit run-or-read instructions."
msgstr "具有明确运行或阅读说明的确定性辅助工具。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:85
msgid "Discovery"
msgstr "发现技能"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:87
msgid ""
"Codex and Claude discover the repository skills automatically through "
"project-native aliases:"
msgstr "Codex 和 Claude 通过项目原生别名自动发现仓库技能："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:95
msgid ""
"Codex scans ``.agents/skills`` and Claude scans ``.claude/skills``. The "
"aliases use the frontmatter ``name`` so both agents expose the same stable "
"identifier. They resolve to the canonical directories under ``skills/``, "
"keeping one maintained copy of each skill and preserving repository-relative"
" references. Do not flatten-copy the skills into a global agent skill "
"directory."
msgstr ""
"Codex 扫描 ``.agents/skills`` ，Claude 扫描 ``.claude/skills`` 。别名使用前置元数据中的 "
"``name`` ，使两个智能体使用同一稳定标识。它们指向 ``skills/`` "
"下的正式目录，使每个技能只维护一份，并保留相对仓库的引用。不要将技能平铺复制到全局智能体技能目录。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:101
msgid ""
"Agents without native skill discovery should use ``skills/README.md`` as the"
" catalog. Select a skill by matching the user's request against the "
"``description`` field in each ``SKILL.md`` frontmatter, then read only that "
"skill and its directly linked files. Directory slugs are canonical file "
"locations for humans and reviewers; the frontmatter ``name`` is the stable "
"identifier to use when one skill routes to another."
msgstr ""
"不支持原生技能发现的智能体应使用 ``skills/README.md`` 作为目录。根据每个 ``SKILL.md`` 前置元数据的 "
"``description`` "
"字段匹配用户请求，再只阅读选中的技能和直接链接的文件。目录名是供人和审阅者使用的正式文件位置；技能互相指引时，应使用前置元数据中的 ``name`` "
"作为稳定标识。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:109
msgid "Skill contract"
msgstr "技能约定"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:111
msgid "Every skill must include a ``SKILL.md`` file with frontmatter:"
msgstr "每个技能必须包含带有前置元数据的 ``SKILL.md`` ："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:122
msgid "The required frontmatter fields are:"
msgstr "前置元数据的必需字段如下："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:124
msgid ""
"Frontmatter intentionally uses a small YAML subset: single-line scalar "
"fields and the ``owners`` list. Do not use block scalars such as ``|`` or "
"``>`` in ``SKILL.md`` frontmatter; keep long details in the markdown body or"
" a linked reference file."
msgstr ""
"前置元数据有意只使用少量 YAML 语法：单行标量字段和 ``owners`` 列表。不要在 ``SKILL.md`` 的前置元数据中使用 ``|`` "
"或 ``>`` 等块标量；较长细节应放在 Markdown 正文或链接的参考文件中。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:128
msgid "``name``"
msgstr "``name``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:129
msgid ""
"Unique lowercase identifier using letters, numbers, and hyphens. Prefer an "
"``isaaclab-`` prefix and avoid generic names such as ``helper``, ``utils``, "
"or ``tools``. The identifier must match the native alias under "
"``.agents/skills/``."
msgstr ""
"由小写字母、数字和连字符组成的唯一标识。建议使用 ``isaaclab-`` 前缀，避免 ``helper`` 、 ``utils`` 、 "
"``tools`` 等泛化名称。标识必须与 ``.agents/skills/`` 下的原生别名一致。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:131
msgid "``description``"
msgstr "``description``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:132
msgid ""
"Third-person discovery text. Include what the skill does and when an agent "
"should use it."
msgstr "用第三人称描述发现技能所需的信息，包括技能做什么，以及智能体何时应使用它。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:134
msgid "Good example:"
msgstr "合适的示例："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:140
msgid "Bad example:"
msgstr "不合适的示例："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:146
msgid "``audience``"
msgstr "``audience``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:147
msgid ""
"Either ``developer`` or ``user``. This must match the directory under "
"``skills/``."
msgstr "取值为 ``developer`` 或 ``user`` ，必须与 ``skills/`` 下的目录一致。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:149
msgid "``status``"
msgstr "``status``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:150
msgid "One of ``experimental``, ``stable``, or ``deprecated``."
msgstr "取值为 ``experimental`` 、 ``stable`` 或 ``deprecated`` 。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:152
msgid ""
"Use ``experimental`` for new or incomplete guidance that still needs real "
"usage. Promote a skill to ``stable`` only after it has maintained "
"references, validation guidance, and review from the owning area. Use "
"``deprecated`` when a workflow is replaced or no longer recommended; "
"deprecated skills must point to the replacement workflow or migration path."
msgstr ""
"新指导或尚不完整、需要实际使用验证的指导，应使用 ``experimental`` "
"。只有具备持续维护的参考资料、验证说明，并经过负责领域的审阅后，才能升为 ``stable`` 。工作流被替代或不再推荐时，使用 "
"``deprecated`` ；已弃用技能必须指向替代工作流或迁移路径。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:154
msgid "``owners``"
msgstr "``owners``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:155
msgid "One or more maintainer groups or owners responsible for the skill."
msgstr "对该技能负责的一个或多个维护者组或负责人。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:157
msgid "Required ``SKILL.md`` sections are:"
msgstr "``SKILL.md`` 必须包含以下章节："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:159
msgid "``When To Use``"
msgstr "``When To Use``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:160
msgid "``Workflow``"
msgstr "``Workflow``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:161
msgid "``Validation``"
msgstr "``Validation``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:162
msgid "``Maintenance``"
msgstr "``Maintenance``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:163
msgid "``References``"
msgstr "``References``"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:165
msgid ""
"User-facing skills must also include an ``evaluations.md`` file with at "
"least three representative scenarios. Each scenario should include a sample "
"prompt or task, expected behavior, and known failure modes or pass/fail "
"criteria."
msgstr ""
"面向用户的技能还必须包含 ``evaluations.md`` "
"，至少提供三个代表性场景。每个场景应包含示例提示词或任务、预期行为，以及已知失败模式或通过与失败的判定标准。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:168
msgid "Authoring guidelines"
msgstr "编写指南"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:170
msgid ""
"These guidelines are adapted from Anthropic's `Skill authoring best "
"practices <https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-"
"skills/best-practices>`_ and tailored to Isaac Lab's documentation and "
"contribution workflow."
msgstr ""
"本指南参考 Anthropic 的 `技能编写最佳实践 <https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-"
"tools/agent-skills/best-practices>`_ ，并根据 Isaac Lab 文档与贡献工作流作了调整。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:172
msgid ""
"Keep ``SKILL.md`` concise. Treat context as shared budget and assume agents "
"already understand general programming concepts. Put only the task-critical "
"workflow in ``SKILL.md``."
msgstr ""
"保持 ``SKILL.md`` 简洁。上下文是共享资源，应假设智能体已理解通用编程概念。 ``SKILL.md`` 只放完成任务必需的工作流。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:174
msgid ""
"Use progressive disclosure. Link directly from ``SKILL.md`` to one-level "
"files such as ``reference.md``, ``examples.md``, or ``evaluations.md``. "
"Avoid chains where ``SKILL.md`` links to a file that links to the actual "
"guidance."
msgstr ""
"逐步提供细节。从 ``SKILL.md`` 直接链接到同一层的 ``reference.md`` 、 ``examples.md`` 或 "
"``evaluations.md`` 等文件。避免通过多个文件跳转，才能找到实际指导。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:176
msgid ""
"Use a contents section for longer references. Reference files over 100 lines"
" should start with ``# Contents`` or ``## Contents`` so agents can navigate "
"them when reading partially."
msgstr ""
"较长参考文件应包含目录。超过 100 行的参考文件应以 ``# Contents`` 或 ``## Contents`` "
"开始，便于智能体在部分阅读时导航。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:178
msgid ""
"Do not include credentials, private content copied from another system, "
"generated logs, hardware-specific benchmark dumps, or large vendored "
"documentation. If that information is useful, summarize the workflow and "
"link to the maintained source instead."
msgstr ""
"不要包含凭据、从其他系统复制的私有内容、生成的日志、特定硬件的基准数据转储，或大份内置第三方文档。如果这些信息有用，应概述工作流并链接到持续维护的来源。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:180
msgid "Set the right degree of freedom:"
msgstr "选择合适的自由度："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:182
msgid "Use high-freedom guidance for reviews and design work."
msgstr "审阅和设计工作使用高自由度指导。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:183
msgid "Use medium-freedom templates when Isaac Lab has a preferred pattern."
msgstr "Isaac Lab 有推荐模式时，使用中等自由度模板。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:184
msgid ""
"Use low-freedom exact commands or scripts for fragile workflows such as "
"validation."
msgstr "验证等容易出错的工作流，使用低自由度的精确命令或脚本。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:186
msgid ""
"Prefer one clear default before listing alternatives. If an escape hatch is "
"needed, state when to use it."
msgstr "先给出一个明确的默认方案，再列出替代方案。如果需要例外路径，说明何时使用。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:188
msgid ""
"Avoid time-sensitive wording. For migrations, use ``Current Workflow`` and "
"``Old Patterns`` sections instead of date-based instructions."
msgstr ""
"避免容易过时的措辞。迁移说明应使用 ``Current Workflow`` 和 ``Old Patterns`` 章节，而不是基于日期的指令。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:190
msgid ""
"Use consistent Isaac Lab terminology throughout a skill, such as ``manager-"
"based environments``, ``event terms``, ``articulation config``, and "
"``changelog fragment``."
msgstr "整个技能使用一致的 Isaac Lab 术语，例如基于管理器的环境、事件项、关节体配置和变更日志片段。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:193
msgid "Keeping skills synchronized"
msgstr "保持技能同步"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:195
msgid ""
"Skills should not become parallel documentation. The source of truth is the "
"Isaac Lab documentation under ``docs/source/`` and the maintained "
"source/examples under ``source/`` and ``scripts/``."
msgstr ""
"技能不应成为另一套独立文档。权威依据是 ``docs/source/`` 下的 Isaac Lab 文档，以及 ``source/`` 、 "
"``scripts/`` 下持续维护的源码和示例。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:197
msgid ""
"Each skill must include a ``Maintenance`` section that names the "
"authoritative files to review when code changes. When a skill needs "
"documentation-level content, update the official docs first and link to them"
" from the skill."
msgstr ""
"每个技能必须包含 ``Maintenance`` 章节，列出代码变更时要复查的权威文件。如果技能需要文档级内容，应先更新官方文档，再从技能链接过去。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:199
msgid ""
"Keep the link bidirectional. When a documentation page under "
"``docs/source/`` is the source of truth for a skill, add a ``.. seealso::`` "
"admonition near the top of that page that names the skill and links back to "
"it. This reminds documentation authors to update the associated skill in the"
" same change, so the two never drift apart. Treat a missing back-link as a "
"review issue whenever a skill's ``Maintenance`` section names a "
"documentation page."
msgstr ""
"保持双向链接。如果 ``docs/source/`` 下某页是技能的权威依据，应在该页开头附近添加 ``.. seealso::`` "
"提示，注明技能名并链接回技能。这能提醒文档作者在同一项修改中更新关联技能，避免二者偏离。技能的 ``Maintenance`` "
"章节列出文档页时，如果文档页没有回链，应在审阅中指出。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:201
msgid "Use these rules during review:"
msgstr "审阅时遵循以下规则："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:203
msgid ""
"Reject large copied API tables or standalone install guides when official "
"docs already cover the topic."
msgstr "如果官方文档已覆盖相关主题，应拒绝大段复制的 API 表格或独立安装指南。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:204
msgid ""
"Prefer links to docs, source files, and maintained examples over duplicated "
"snippets."
msgstr "优先链接到文档、源码和持续维护的示例，避免重复代码片段。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:205
msgid ""
"Keep only agent-specific value in the skill: routing, task sequencing, "
"validation loops, search terms, and known decision points."
msgstr "技能只保留对智能体有针对性价值的内容：指引、任务顺序、验证循环、搜索词和已知决策点。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:206
msgid ""
"If a skill uncovers a missing migration note or troubleshooting entry, add "
"that note to ``docs/source/`` rather than expanding the skill."
msgstr "如果技能暴露了缺失的迁移说明或故障排查条目，应将其添加到 ``docs/source/`` ，而不是扩充技能。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:207
msgid ""
"For simulation, asset, sensor, or randomization workflows, state whether the"
" guidance is backend-neutral or specific to PhysX, Newton, or a "
"renderer/visualizer backend. Link to the multi-backend docs and source "
"implementations instead of copying backend tables into the skill."
msgstr ""
"对于仿真、资产、传感器或随机化工作流，应说明指导是否适用于所有后端，还是只适用于 PhysX、Newton "
"或某个渲染、可视化后端。应链接到多后端文档和源码实现，而不是将后端表格复制到技能中。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:208
msgid "Run the skill validator after every skill change."
msgstr "每次修改技能后，都运行技能验证器。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:211
msgid "Validation workflow"
msgstr "验证流程"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:213
msgid "Validate skills locally with:"
msgstr "在本地使用以下命令验证技能："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:219
msgid ""
"The validator checks frontmatter, required sections, unique names, "
"audience/path consistency, link validity, reference depth, portable paths, "
"native Codex and Claude aliases, required user evaluations, minimum "
"evaluation scenario counts, and per-scenario evaluation details such as "
"sample queries, expected behavior, and known failure modes or pass/fail "
"criteria."
msgstr ""
"验证器检查前置元数据、必需章节、名称唯一性、受众与路径的一致性、链接有效性、参考层级、路径可移植性、原生 Codex 和 Claude "
"别名、必需的用户评估、评估场景最少数量，以及各场景的示例查询、预期行为、已知失败模式或判定标准等细节。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:221
msgid "Run the validator tests with:"
msgstr "使用以下命令运行验证器测试："

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:227
msgid ""
"The skills CI gate runs only when a pull request changes files under "
"``skills/``, ``tools/skills/``, or the skills workflow. This keeps unrelated"
" Isaac Lab PRs from being blocked by skill validation while still checking "
"validator changes."
msgstr ""
"技能 CI 检查仅在 PR 修改 ``skills/`` 、 ``tools/skills/`` "
"或技能工作流时运行。这样既能检查验证器变更，也不会因技能验证阻止无关的 Isaac Lab PR。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:230
msgid "Review policy"
msgstr "审阅规则"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:232
msgid ""
"Developer skills require maintainer approval from the owning area because "
"they affect contributor workflows."
msgstr "开发者技能影响贡献者工作流，需要负责领域的维护者批准。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:234
msgid ""
"User skills require maintained references, a validation path, documentation "
"alignment, and at least three evaluation scenarios."
msgstr "用户技能必须具备持续维护的参考资料、验证方式、与文档的一致性，以及至少三个评估场景。"

#: source/developer-tools/agent_skills.rst:236
msgid ""
"Reviewers should reject skills that duplicate general knowledge instead of "
"encoding Isaac Lab-specific workflow. Deprecated skills must include "
"migration guidance and a replacement skill when one exists."
msgstr ""
"技能如果只是重复通用知识，而没有说明 Isaac Lab 专用工作流，审阅者应拒绝它。已弃用技能必须提供迁移说明；有替代技能时，也必须注明。"
